/-!
# Cyclic compatibility of disjoint annular crosscuts

The Jordan-theta theorem says that the two complementary separators built
from a pair of crosscuts fill the outer disk.  This file extracts the order
statement needed for finite shell cells: once the side containing the inner
disk is fixed, every third disjoint crosscut has its two endpoints on the
corresponding complementary boundary arcs.
-/

namespace Schoenflies

open Set Function
open LeanEval.Topology.ClassificationOfSurfaces.Moise

